      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-249736",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/4c/4cc9c0bd1164bc246beaafdfd0a5326d82556aa49bbffd910145351e572084d7.png)\n\nSuppose we fix the following order of the vertices in the above graph: $v_{1}$, $v_{2}$, $v_{3}$, $v_{4}$, $v_{5}, v_{6}, v_{7}, v_{8}$.\nThe breadth-first search algorithm is applied to the graph, starting at $v_{5}$. After considering all the vertices that are connected to $v_{5}$, we have the following configuration, where the queue and the array of visited vertices are ordered from left to right:\n\n| Queue: | $v_{3}$, $v_{4}$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Visited: | $v_{5}$, $v_{3}$, $v_{4}$ |\n\nThe vertices visited by the algorithm on the next iteration are\n{{field-1}}."
